    <string name="plugin_tip_title">Tip: get the most out of the replace button</string>
    <string name="plugin_tip_body">The "replace next track" button works right away, but picks smarter tracks if your Lyrion server has SugarCube or RandomFlow (pick which one in Settings) and/or Don\'t Stop The Music installed. Without them, it still works fine using a plain random pick from the same genre or artist.\n\nUsing Squeezelite as your player? This app works great as its companion, controlling playback while Squeezelite runs quietly in the background.</string>
    <string name="volume_tip_title">Tip: volume slider</string>
    <string name="volume_tip_body">Press down on the remote from the player buttons and a volume slider appears. Left and right change the volume (the step is set in Settings), OK mutes. A few seconds after you move away it disappears again. Whether the volume buttons on your remote control the player depends on your setup. If they don\'t, use the slider instead.\n\nThe slider only shows for players whose volume can be changed, so not for players that are fixed at 100%.\n\nDon\'t turn up your TV, receiver or speakers to make up for a low slider: other sources will then play too loud.\n\nAfter a while without input, the focus always returns to the play/pause button.</string>
    <string name="plugin_tip_ok">Got it</string>

